{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations","id":934774,"title":"Mage Populations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-20T16:43:05-07:00","id":934774,"title":"Mage Populations","content":"So, I was looking at Sorcerer (Revised) the other day and, on page 31, it mentioned that the Technocracy depended on its Extraordinary Scientists (Sorcerers) to do most of the grunt work because it had only hundreds of Enlightened members. If there are only hundreds of Awakened members of the Technocracy, I would suggest that there are only thousands of Mages across the world and that mages are one-in-a-million. I think that the vast majority of the 'magic' that occurs in WoD is Numina. I do not mind, however, Numina practitioners being one out of five hundred (0.2%) of the population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T20:48:50-07:00","id":934887,"title":"","content":"Only hundreds? That doesn't sound right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:32:06-07:00","id":934902,"title":"","content":"I have not been able to find any estimates of numbers from any other book. Anyway, it would explain why the Technocracy has not been able to eliminate 'reality deviants', they lack the Enlightened manpower and have to rely on Extraordinary Citizens to do everything. Extraordinary citizens would use Scientific Numina to change the paradigm and Enlightened members would guide them and take out any threats to the new paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T02:54:07-07:00","id":934973,"title":"","content":"We had a thread about this: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...the-traditions</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T05:47:58-07:00","id":935010,"title":"","content":"I do not practice necromancy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> The reason why I have brought it up is to discuss the consequences of having only around seven thousand Mages in existence. I think that you could have the WoD with those numbers as long as you had around fourteen million Sorcerers of various types also practicing magic (ranging in capabilities of one level to Numina on up). Of course, this is assuming that the majority of people who say they have powers (magical, psychic, scientific, etc) have just one level of Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:29:06-07:00","id":935094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=935010#post935010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not practice necromancy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> The reason why I have brought it up is to discuss the consequences of having only around seven thousand Mages in existence. I think that you could have the WoD with those numbers as long as you had around fourteen million Sorcerers of various types also practicing magic (ranging in capabilities of one level to Numina on up). Of course, this is assuming that the majority of people who say they have powers (magical, psychic, scientific, etc) have just one level of Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple. Toss pretty much the flluff whole game out the window. No need for anything above the Sect level really. Factions become more like &quot;loose working groups&quot;. Like super-cabals, effectively. Any organization below that goes out the window. (There aren't enough members of the Order of Hermes to divide up into Houses, for example. There would be less than 10 in a largish House. And don't even try to address all the Methodologies and sub-Methodologies out the window... The sum total of &quot;necronaut&quot; VE's would be about equal to the Ghostbusters..) The Ascension War becomes a lot less about controlling the Destiny of Humanity and scales down to more maneuvering to keep each group's &quot;whatever&quot; optimal. (The Technocracy to influence relevant parts of civilzation but other groups might be manuvering to be left alone. Keeping everyone OUT of Shangri-La is more the point...) A LOT more Orphans unless it becomes much easier to detect who is going to Awaken. Then the game has a large &quot;Mage the Recruitment&quot; aspect as nascent mages are so valuable to the Sorcerer-heavy or teensey-tiny all-Awakened groups out there. If Awakening is as mysterious and unpredictable as it currently is portrayed, most mages are going to have to figure it out on their own until they bump up against one of the established groups.<br /> <br /> And so on...<br /> <br /> Which isn't a bad game, but it's definitely not what is portrayed. <br /> <br /> Using the whole idea of the world actually be <i><b>SORCERERS </b></i><span style=\"font-size:9px\">(+ some mages)</span> is roughly the same as trying to play VtM using the 1 vamp/100,000 rule and expecting to have the cities look ANYTHING like way they are depicted in the fluff . It's pretty ludicrous(with very,very few exceptions for the biggest cities in the world) . Most largest cities in the US will have a few coteries at best. A Clan meeting will be a few folks. Like nuclear family sized. There is no need for all those offices, unless vampires are so self-important that half to all of the vamp population of the city have a title. A city of 1,000,000 people has 10 vampires. So one coterie is the Prince, the Seneshal, the Sheriff, the Scourge and the one poor vamp that doesn't get a title. And the other coterie is effectively &quot;the Oppressed&quot;. And so on. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:27:24-07:00","id":935122,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is pretty much how I have always figured the Mages and the other supernaturals. Look at the Garou and the Fera. The Garou are supposed to be only 1:500,000 and the Fera might be 1:500,000 (though the Nagah and the Nuwisha are nearly extinct while the Ratkin are much more common that any suspects). Given the breeding dynamics of the Garou and the majority of the Fera, a realistic assessment should put their Human Kinfolk at one hundred times their numbers and their Animal Kinfolk at twenty times their numbers (Ratkin have their own rules because they are created by the Birthing Plague), so Werewolf should be <i><b>Kinfolk</b></i> (<span style=\"font-size:8px\">+ some werewolves</span>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:23:38-07:00","id":943517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=935094#post935094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simple. Toss pretty much the flluff whole game out the window. No need for anything above the Sect level really. Factions become more like &quot;loose working groups&quot;. Like super-cabals, effectively. Any organization below that goes out the window. (There aren't enough members of the Order of Hermes to divide up into Houses, for example. There would be less than 10 in a largish House. And don't even try to address all the Methodologies and sub-Methodologies out the window... The sum total of &quot;necronaut&quot; VE's would be about equal to the Ghostbusters..) The Ascension War becomes a lot less about controlling the Destiny of Humanity and scales down to more maneuvering to keep each group's &quot;whatever&quot; optimal. (The Technocracy to influence relevant parts of civilzation but other groups might be manuvering to be left alone. Keeping everyone OUT of Shangri-La is more the point...) A LOT more Orphans unless it becomes much easier to detect who is going to Awaken. Then the game has a large &quot;Mage the Recruitment&quot; aspect as nascent mages are so valuable to the Sorcerer-heavy or teensey-tiny all-Awakened groups out there. If Awakening is as mysterious and unpredictable as it currently is portrayed, most mages are going to have to figure it out on their own until they bump up against one of the established groups.<br /> <br /> And so on...<br /> <br /> Which isn't a bad game, but it's definitely not what is portrayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually, I was reading through the 1E OoH book the other day and apparently most of the &quot;Houses&quot; are made up of a handful of Mages. House Tytalus has 4 cabals. (which I assume number somewhere between 3-5 members each) House Thig had like 1 surviving cabal hanging out on Doissetep. So, the numbers, at least originally, really don't seem to be that huge. So, can see most members of various groups just being mid to high level sorcerers if the ST wants that. Not like Sorcerers can't kick serious ass if pushed. They're really not that &quot;linear&quot; despite the name Mages put on them either. Most of the Paths are quite versatile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:08:58-07:00","id":943571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>angryicecream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=943517#post943517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually, I was reading through the 1E OoH book the other day and apparently most of the &quot;Houses&quot; are made up of a handful of Mages. House Tytalus has 4 cabals. (which I assume number somewhere between 3-5 members each) House Thig had like 1 surviving cabal hanging out on Doissetep. So, the numbers, at least originally, really don't seem to be that huge. So, can see most members of various groups just being mid to high level sorcerers if the ST wants that. Not like Sorcerers can't kick serious ass if pushed. They're really not that &quot;linear&quot; despite the name Mages put on them either. Most of the Paths are quite versatile.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> this has basically been retconned to 1 mage per 200.000 people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> also by the way concerning vampire population. the 1 per 100000 works much better if you care to remember that all these vampires are concentrated in cities .<br /> <br /> <br /> there's no such thing as a vampire living at once in 10 cities with 10.000 people each.<br /> <br /> plus some cities just have a larger population. of vampires. while others have a bit smaller.<br /> <br /> <br /> for the same reason that london is bigger than manchester","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:19:30-07:00","id":943633,"title":"","content":"Where can I find the retcon? I would like to know for reference sake in case I ever run another Mage game. I think I will keep to the old population myself and just have a lot of Sorcerers. I am uncomfortable with more than 7000 nascent gods playing with reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:51:38-07:00","id":943685,"title":"","content":"Then you'll be playing a game that is pretty far removed from the setting as it is presented in pretty much every way, EXCEPT for some really badly thought out population numbers back in the very very beginning. No real cabals. There aren't enough True Mages for them. True Mages are going to be precious flowers that need to be protected and cultivated by their specific groups until they are one-person powerhouses or Bond villain types. No group is going to waste a potential asset of that caliber by having them run around and get in dangerous situations. The game would probably entail a whole lot of trying to capture the recently Awakened and then locking them down for &quot;education&quot;. Probably with a lot of attempts to find and extract young mages from their &quot;creches&quot;. <br /> <br /> As you said, they're nascent gods. What group of Sorcerers is going to waste that kind of potential by allowing them to go out and &quot;adventure&quot;? It''ll be like playing a Vampire game where the PCs are all neonates of very low generation. They're just too vulnerable and precious to allow them to do interesting things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T10:35:50-07:00","id":943703,"title":"","content":"I take my numbers from Sorcerer (Revised). If you have a more recent book with more accurate numbers, please share the book and page number. I generally think that it is difficult to prevent Mages from doing anything, at least if you want them to continue working with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T11:02:14-07:00","id":943720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=943703#post943703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take my numbers from Sorcerer (Revised). If you have a more recent book with more accurate numbers, please share the book and page number. I generally think that it is difficult to prevent Mages from doing anything, at least if you want them to continue working with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should consider those numbers to be what I call 'White Wolf canon.' That is to say, canon that's so stupid that you should just ignore it, as it doesn't fit either the setting or common sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T11:45:44-07:00","id":943751,"title":"","content":"Which is another way of saying 'no book, no page' or, to put it another way, 'home brewed numbers pulled from one's rear end'. How is it stupid that there are only 7,000 Mages? With instantaneous communication and teleportation, you could have the members of a Circle living across the United States without much trouble. <br /> <br /> I do not think that there could be 35,000 Mages globally without the very fabric of reality on Earth starting to fray at the edges. The Marauder populations would be in the thousands rather than the hundreds. Instead of Marauders working in small groups, dozens of Marauders would be working together. It is hard to imagine how much damage sixty Quiet 3 Marauders could do to a major city in an hour. Manhattan would be transformed into an abattoir as they could summon and release twenty-four thousand Umbrood within that amount of time. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy and the Traditions could not stop them, the Quiet of the Marauders gives non-Marauders Mages the paradox that they are generating, and their sorcerer allies in the local area would be overwhelmed. Mundane resources would be overwhelmed within minutes and, even though the Quiet would reset the frame of the world from the delusion of the Marauders to the real world when they leave, the Umbrood would still be running around without supervision. It could easy take days or weeks to hunt down and destroy the Umbrood and, by that time, there would be no doubt to the existence of the supernatural. <br /> <br /> Now, if the desire is for a world where entire cities disappear without explanation once a year, then 35,000 Mages would be suitable. If the desire is for a world more like ours, a world of darkness, then I do not think that there can be a larger population of Mages just because of the Marauder problem. When the problems that would occur if the number of Nephandi were thousands instead of hundreds are added into the equation, then a smaller population of Mages makes much more sense than a larger population of Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:06:39-07:00","id":943805,"title":"","content":"No page doesn't matter when it completely invalidates the setting as presented to keep with BS numbers that literally make no sense. It's just as bad as Vampire, where 1:100,000 negates much of the rest of the setting. Even the largest cities don't have enough vamps for any real politics, much less a raft of titles and duties LARGE cities have a dozen vamps. You have to have an actual metropolis to even get started on inter-coterie rivalries. Clans aren't political or social organizations, they're nuclear families. Even &quot;this city is over-populated&quot; falls flat when every city has to be &quot;over-populated&quot; to have enough vampires to have anything relevant to happen.<br /> <br /> Mage with 1:1,000,000 is pretty much the same. You don't NEED most groupings with that few mages. They are so thin on the ground, most are going to be Orphans. Those that aren't are going to be in fairly small groups. Traditions and Conventions would pretty much be cabals with similar Foci within the Sects. A cabal of mages is a BIG deal, as even a small group is actually a measurable fraction of ALL the Mages there are. <br /> <br /> People don't need to cite &quot;this page in this book&quot; to refute the 1:1,000,000 concept. They can cite entire BOOKS that refute it. Every cabal presented. Pretty much all the history and background in every book. Every stab at a setting books (Chantries, Horizon, Las Vegas). Hells, there are too many NPCs in the first adventure for San Francisco to hold comfortably (not the one with the statue crying blood with the screen, the one with the spiders). It's embedded into the matrix of the game's rules where PCs aren't portrayed as the vanishingly rare super-special snowflakes they would be under the &quot;mages are SOOOOOOOO super rare&quot; regime.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you don't have to work too hard to refute the whole &quot;the difference is Sorcerers&quot; either. Since, as has been pointed out, I can't think of a many NPC as having been depicted as having risen up from Sorcerers to Mages. Nor have cabals been depicted as being composed of mostly Sorcerers. Nor have Chantries been depicted as being full of Sorcerer personnel with a few true mages sprinkled in. Sure it SAYS that over here in this one place, but, from the get-go, that was a double-take moment. When it came out, people said &quot;Huh?&quot;, not &quot;Oh, finally! Now it all makes SENSE!&quot; <br /> <br /> You can always do what you want in your own game. It's not a bad way to do it, if you want to make the relevant changes. Like, why are there this many fairly newly minted mages thrown together to form the cabal of PCs? Statistically, it would be quite an aberration for this many mages of this many different groups at this level of expertise to all be thrown together instead of working within the matrix of Sorcerers that make up the entirety of their respective Sects. Make sure the character's meet few mages as opposition. It should be Sorcerers when it's &quot;like vs. like&quot; unless that's the whole point of the encounter (e.g. the are meeting the &quot;dark mirror&quot; version of their group, or this is the &quot;BIG BAD&quot; for this portion of the chronicle). You will need to retool the way that various groups are presented and probably use spirits and other supernaturals extensively. Most of the &quot;Darkness&quot; of the World of Darkness isn't mages in this setting, so the PCs are going to be banging elbows against the more common supers of other flavors. And so on.<br /> <br /> What it won't be is the setting described in pretty much all the books and supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:42:33-07:00","id":944055,"title":"","content":"Except that they do not. Horizon contained only 150 Mages, including visitors, and it was the center of the Traditions (Horizon - Stronghold of Hope, p. 59). If Horizon, the largest stronghold of the Traditions in the Umbra, possesses only 150 Mages on average, how many Mages can there actually be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T03:17:17-07:00","id":944212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=943633#post943633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find the retcon? I would like to know for reference sake in case I ever run another Mage game. I think I will keep to the old population myself and just have a lot of Sorcerers. I am uncomfortable with more than 7000 nascent gods playing with reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i believe it was fallen tower las vegas which says 1 mystic per 150000 people<br /> <br /> however malcolm sheppard clarified this includes sorcerers.<br /> <br /> and then said that in order for enough mages to exist he also believes that a lot of sorcerers fall &quot;off the radar&quot; e.g the guys who have just 1 or 2 dots in sorcery paths are too weak to count<br /> <br /> thus 1 mage per 200.000","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T04:14:19-07:00","id":944233,"title":"","content":"Quote from FTLV:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the first challenges a Storyteller faces when creat-<br /> ing a Mage setting is deciding just how many <b>mages</b> exist<br /> among the masses of <b>Sleepers</b>. White Wolf uses a rough<br /> rule of thumb of one <b>mage</b> per 150,000 people, though<br /> this should be readily broken in order to promote story. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T05:29:43-07:00","id":944252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=944233#post944233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quote from FTLV:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> yeah i know the words mages was used. it's just that the guy who wrote this considered mages and sorcerers to be one and the same when writing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T06:23:05-07:00","id":944269,"title":"","content":"Which would make sorcerers ludicrously rare. I have been closely associated with five dozen people that practice magic and met ten times that number that practiced magic, and they were just in the Chapel Hill region of North Carolina. Now, most of them were not skilled practitioners, they would have had the equivalent of one level in one Path, but they were practitioners of magic. I doubt that practitioners of magic are going to be less common in WoD than in real life.<br /> <br /> Before anyone starts arguing that magic does not exist in real life, that would be the same argument that a Sleeper in the world of darkness would make. Does magic exist in the real world? Yes. Is it effective? No, not for the most part. The vast majority of practitioners would be better off taking up tennis because they would at least get some exercise. Is there anything like a Mage in the real world? No, not as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T07:07:13-07:00","id":944288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=944269#post944269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would make sorcerers ludicrously rare. I have been closely associated with five dozen people that practice magic and met ten times that number that practiced magic, and they were just in the Chapel Hill region of North Carolina. Now, most of them were not skilled practitioners, they would have had the equivalent of one level in one Path, but they were practitioners of magic. I doubt that practitioners of magic are going to be less common in WoD than in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now you made the WoD Sorcerors more common than postmen.<br /> Because, really, you just basically said that there are hundreds of magic practitioners in a roughly 4.5 x 4.5 mile area.<br /> Or essentially 1% of the local population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T08:19:00-07:00","id":944329,"title":"","content":"Chapel Hill region is more than the town of Chapel Hill. It is anyone within the Research Triangle Area, which is a population of around 2 million people, though I am sure that I did not meet more than a fraction of people who practiced magic. I would say that the entire magic practicing population of the region was around 0.1%. Now, you can just say that they were just people who believed that they practiced magic if that would make you feel more comfortable. Either way, people who practice magic (or believe they practice magic if you prefer) are much, much more common than the general public would like to admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T08:48:26-07:00","id":944342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=944329#post944329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapel Hill region is more than the town of Chapel Hill. It is anyone within the Research Triangle Area, which is a population of around 2 million people, though I am sure that I did not meet more than a fraction of people who practiced magic. I would say that the entire magic practicing population of the region was around 0.1%</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That quite changes things.<br /> Still, that would equal around 1 in 1000. Let's say that even in the WoD, most of them don't practice 'real' magic and make the actual Sorceror/Psychic ratio with *some* accurate occult knowledge or affliction (conciously or not) 0,01%. So, 1 in 10000. Which makes numbers like 1 proper Mage in 250,000 sound quite reasonable again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-05-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:35:41-07:00","id":944428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=944269#post944269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, most of them were not skilled practitioners, they would have had the equivalent of one level in one Path, but they were practitioners of magic. I doubt that practitioners of magic are going to be less common in WoD than in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I would argue that most of those people have the equivalent of zero dots in any paths. Probably just a couple of dots in Occult would cover it. Actual magic should be hard to come by in the World of Darkness. If it was as wide spread as you say than everyone would have some.<br /> <br /> The numbers I usually use are a compromise between the 1 in a million and 1 in 150,000. I use about 11,000 mages (1 in 590,000 people) and 3 times as many numina users (which includes sorcerers, psychics, faith users etc). Sorcery is usually the most common since it can theoretically be learned. Faith and Psychic abilities shouldn't be teachable imo.<br /> <br /> At least for me, those numbers worked out fine for the games I ran.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:42:39-07:00","id":944432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=944055#post944055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that they do not. Horizon contained only 150 Mages, including visitors, and it was the center of the Traditions (Horizon - Stronghold of Hope, p. 59). If Horizon, the largest stronghold of the Traditions in the Umbra, possesses only 150 Mages on average, how many Mages can there actually be?</div> </div> </div> </div>150 Mages in Horizon, out of a population of 30,000. I don't see any figures given on the sorcerer population (and, according to the systems you propose there should be 100's, definitely enough to leave a footprint that couldn't be simply ignored). Effectively, Horizon isn't much of a Chantry/Horizon Realm and it admits it outright. It's the Brasilia of Chantries. Largely a show piece demonstrating the &quot;unity&quot; of the 9 Traditions, set up, then sorta left empty (mostly howling wilderness) and used for emblematic and political purposes. (Though all 9 of those Nodes are going to need cabals to guard them as well. Probably small-ish Chantries in their own right). <br /> <br /> After all, Doisstetep has 10 cabals and 50 members, only two of which are Disciple status in the &quot;young blood&quot; group, meaning that there are other apprentices (Initiates and Disciples) that aren't even counted as they don't belong to their Mentor's cabal and, being a dependent, aren't forming cabals of their own. And, though it's the biggest Chantry (aside from Horizon), it's not the only big Chantry out there. The Rank 3 Chantries seem to have about a dozen members and those shouldn't even comparatively rare. And Rank has a component of &quot;fame&quot; as well, as a Rank 0 hidden Chantry has 20 members. And that doesn't include mages that aren't directly affiliated with a Chantry.<br /> <br /> And that's just for the Traditions. The Union is even bigger. Plus everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:06:36-07:00","id":944511,"title":"","content":"Alright, let us say that you have a Mage population of 1:100,000. That would mean that there are 70,000 nascent gods on Earth. Now, while there are not any hard numbers, let us assume that 40% of them are Independent, 20% of them are Tradition, 20% of them are Technomancer, 10% of them are Marauder, and 10% of them are Nephandi. That would mean that there are 7,000 Marauders on Earth.<br /> <br /> Let us ignore the other populations and look at the Marauder population. Marauders range from Quiet 1 to 5, with Quiet 1 being Dark Knight Batman and Quiet 5 being Alice in Wonderland Mad Hatter. In general, Quiet 3 seems to be the average Quiet for someone who goes Marauder, so we will break down the Marauder population to be 10% Quiet 1, 20% Quiet 2, 40% Quiet 3, 20% Quiet 4, and 10% Quiet 5. While the other Marauders are problematic, let us ignore them for now and focus on Quiet 5 Marauders. That would mean that there were 700 Quiet 5 Marauders on Earth.<br /> <br /> It is difficult to conceive of the damage that one Quiet 5 Marauder can do. They are capable of ignoring 15 points of Backlash per turn and, what is worse, the Paradox does not go away, it effects the local population (first, the Awakened, next, the UnAwakened). A Quiet 5 Marauder can do practically anything they want and, while reality will try to reweave things to fit within the Consensus after they have left, the people are still dead and the buildings are still destroyed. With 700 Quiet 5 Marauders, you could have groups of Quiet 5 Marauders running around the Earth because the Avatars of Marauders are capable of communicating even if their Mages are not. You would literally start having groups of dozens of Quiet 5 Marauders destroying entire cities every day and, within a year, I doubt that there would be enough human beings alive who did not believe in magic to maintain the Consensus.<br /> <br /> The reason why Mages need a low population (and why sorcerers need a high population) is because Mages are actually nascent gods (the game should have really been called Divinity: the Apotheoses) and sorcerers are actually the magicians. A Mage population of 1:1,000,000 might allow a world that resembles ours enough to be a world of darkness. A Mage population of 1:100,000 would make the Marvel's Universe seem logical and tame by comparison.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:49:59-07:00","id":944577,"title":"","content":"Your number crunching it's biased...<br /> <br /> Because:<br /> 1.<br /> You shouldn't count 700 Madness 5 Marauders on earth because many could be in the Umbra. Being a Marauder doesn't suddenly make you unable to Step Sideways , or live in the Umbra (and since being long periods of time in the Umbra it's one big cause mages becoming Marauders, I say that there should be a fairly large number of them there by free will)<br /> <br /> So, it's 700 Marauders in the Universe, not only in Earth<br /> <br /> 2.<br /> Marauder Quiet range from 1 to 10, not from 1 to 5. Marauders above 5 get send to the Umbra, and can't return to earth (I don't remember if lvl 5 Marauders got sended too).<br /> <br /> So, your numbers are wrong...<br /> <br /> 3.<br /> Let's say that there's 400 Madness 5/4 on Earth<br /> <br /> Having a high Quiet does not equal having a big capacity to alter the background. A Marauder's Avatar uses the Sphere lvl of the Mage to do that. The Mage also needs Spheres to do stuff.<br /> You ain't going to destroy that much with low level Spheres and Technocrats, Traditionalists and even Nephandy hunting you down (as Marauders have the rather unfortunate trait of being everyone's enemies). You need Spirit 4 just to release a monster that can't or won't materialize by itself...<br /> <br /> So, only a minority of these mages are going to be able to wreak havok in largue scale before being stopped by the forces that watch this sort of things.<br /> <br /> Let's say 60 have what it takes to be a world changer.<br /> <br /> 3.<br /> Marauders motives are unfathomable. Just like Avatar's motives are. Marauders aren't all friends of each other, and frictions among it's &quot;files&quot; aren't unheard off. Not all Marauders are equaly &quot;noisy&quot; with their magick, and they most certainly aren't going to join in massive cabals all the time.<br /> <br /> There's no real reason to think they all will form cabals, the loner marauder it's, in fact, as common if not more than the cabal or &quot;faction&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let's say 30 of these powerful Marauders form 30 or so cabals (joining with minnor Marauders) and are interested in trashing stuff.<br /> <br /> 4.<br /> The world it's BIG. The 30 cabals could easily have Four countries for each one, and still there would be countries free of powerful marauder Cabals.<br /> <br /> 5.<br /> There are &quot;only&quot; 1 mage per 200.000/150.000 people, so the numbers are even smaller (let's say 15 Cabals of Marauders of REAL impact).<br /> <br /> And these cabals will have entire FACTIONS or mages hunting them (and other people too). They will have to move very carefully or be destroyed rather quickly. Cabals that don't know how to hide WILL be wiped from the face of the earth, because mages can take a bit of Paradox, if it means to kill these powerful threats, and can wipe a few millons of minds, if such a feat isn't needed everyday.<br /> <br /> SO, no, I don't see how a few thousands of Marauders are going to destroy the world, specially since not all of them even care, and there's tens of thousands of Techoncrats (and Traditionalist's too, in this case) to clean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason why Mages need a low population (and why sorcerers need a high population) is because Mages are actually nascent gods (the game should have really been called Divinity: the Apotheoses) and sorcerers are actually the magicians. A Mage population of 1:1,000,000 might allow a world that resembles ours enough to be a world of darkness. A Mage population of 1:100,000 would make the Marvel's Universe seem logical and tame by comparison. </div> </div> </div>This it's your head canon. I can see it working very well. I can see that it's appealing. But it isn't really mandatory to make sense of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-05-2016, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:30:10-07:00","id":944610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=944577#post944577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This it's your head canon. I can see it working very well. I can see that it's appealing. But it isn't really mandatory to make sense of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It can work. Two ways actually. <br /> <br /> 1. Make the adjustments to make the &quot;mage-scarce&quot; world you're seeing as I've previously mentioned. Or any one of a number of ways of doing so with a little creative acumen applied to the relevant boundary considerations. <br /> <br /> 2. You (meaning Aya) can just handwave the numbers and run the game the way it's written, internal inconsistency warts and all. Keep the numbers it says with mage population, the number of sorcerers mentioned in a couple of places (and never disavowed because disavowal has been, apparently tantamount to rank cowardice in WW game development) and the fact that the setting as a whole is all about groups of mages with few to no sorcerers... and run a cabal of mages and their associated mages, (who are not-insignificant fraction of all the mages there are) the way that the entire rest of the game on every level functions/is depicted/etc. There's actually no problem with this. Internal homeostatic consistency isn't required if your story doesn't need it I've run over a dozen mage games since the mid-90's and I've seldom worried about statistical integrity in my mage demographics. <br /> <br /> Another thing... this &quot;nascent gods&quot; thing.... That's taking a specific and somewhat permissive viewpoint on what mages can accomplish and how that pans out. Depending on how you run Paradox, things may not be all that easy and the consequences of failure may fall on the mage more than on the environment (the difference between Marauders and everyone else). Depending on how you scale effects, it's probably not all that easy to do things that manifest on a large scale or create overtly massive changes to the environment. To do magnificent and terrible things will often take 4 or 5 dot effects and Adepts and Masters don't have to be any more common than elder vampires or high ranking werewolves are in their respective societies. (And there's the whole &quot;retreat to the Umbra&quot; factor reducing the chance Masters are actually handing out on Earth proper).<br /> <br /> A Mage using Correspondence 3 to teleport isn't going to break the world, even if he does it at midfield during the Superbowl. Turning lead into gold with Matter 3 isn't an existential threat to reality or even to the economy, (particularly since your enemies are specifically looking for you to try crap like that). Neither will making a car break down (Entropy 3), doing a Vulcan mind meld (Mind 3), etc. <br /> <br /> I've actually been somewhat underwhelmed by what characters do when they aren't full on at 100% maximum creativity. There are LOTS of limitations: Spheres needed (even worse with the rampant Sphere bloat in HDYDT), number of dots needed, number of successes needed, Difficulty modified (and the max/min really hurts here more than it helps), possibility of Paradox (including the danger of that already incurred), and, lest we forget, the fact that almost all of that has to be shoehorned into Focus (though that can get Purpled away, but not at the level many games run). And then there's when the dice don't play nice. <br /> <br /> I don't think these guys are as powerful as you seem to believe they are.... They CAN be, when all cylinders are firing, but that's not necessarily the &quot;default&quot; setting. Otherwise, it's not really much of a game. No real conflict and no real danger is pretty much no real plot and no opportunity for growth and development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T18:30:01-07:00","id":944635,"title":"","content":"I'm hesitant to set down a definitive number of mages in my games. I want there to be enough of them to fill out the ranks of the various groups, yet few enough that player-characters are important and have the potential to change the world significantly. I'm not sure there's any real number that can represent this. Maybe an imaginary number? Let's call it 15,000i.<br /> <br /> On Sorcerers. I think the best way to include them, and in numbers much larger than those of mages, is to make them suck a lot more. They'd be just barely distinguishable from your real-life Asatru cousin who draws runes on stuff and thinks it helps him at gambling. The traces of belief their rituals feed off are almost nonexistent, and so should be their magic. But occasionally they'd get lucky, probably just enough to get them in trouble. The only real way for them to wield a lot of power would be diabolism. But even that should probably be toned down--manifesting the power of unspeakable otherworldly evil is covered pretty well by the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Edit: I realized it's a bit weird that Nephandi are true mages. I'll have to give that more thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 08-05-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T10:33:21-07:00","id":944935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=944610#post944610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've actually been somewhat underwhelmed by what characters do when they aren't full on at 100% maximum creativity. There are LOTS of limitations: Spheres needed (even worse with the rampant Sphere bloat in HDYDT), number of dots needed, number of successes needed, Difficulty modified (and the max/min really hurts here more than it helps), possibility of Paradox (including the danger of that already incurred), and, lest we forget, the fact that almost all of that has to be shoehorned into Focus (though that can get Purpled away, but not at the level many games run). And then there's when the dice don't play nice.<br /> <br /> I don't think these guys are as powerful as you seem to believe they are.... They CAN be, when all cylinders are firing, but that's not necessarily the &quot;default&quot; setting. Otherwise, it's not really much of a game. No real conflict and no real danger is pretty much no real plot and no opportunity for growth and development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, that's more of a feature than a glitch to me.<br /> <br /> Magic is a toolbox. It's a toolbox that grants you nigh on Omnipotence. But it's still a toolbox in the hands of a flawed person. That person isn't GOING to use it perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:07:48-07:00","id":945119,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree with that.<br /> <br /> One could add that one of the reasons Marauders are so scary it's that they can suddenly sidestep those difficulties. They can (sometimes, at the storyteller's discretion) cast with more Spheres than normal, ignore huge amounts of Paradox, join in groups with seemingly contradictory agendas or Paradigms, and use really bizarre Focus that defy common sense.<br /> <br /> They're crazy, but they're also controled by magical forces that even mages can't truly understand which can make them act in unpredictable ways and maybe even break (or abuse) some of the rules. But I think that this loses it's appeal if it's taken for granted.<br /> Marauders are as powerful as weak. Their madness gives them strenght, but also limits and defines what they can and will do. They may be tools of their Avatars, but that doesn't mean that they all follow a common agenda...or, if they do, it's so metaphysical and big that it doesn't imply teamwork as we normally understand it (without being agains't it), and so arcane that can't be easily predicted by average mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:36:49-07:00","id":959032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations#post934774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was looking at Sorcerer (Revised) the other day and, on page 31, it mentioned that the Technocracy depended on its Extraordinary Scientists (Sorcerers) to do most of the grunt work because it had only hundreds of Enlightened members. If there are only hundreds of Awakened members of the Technocracy, I would suggest that there are only thousands of Mages across the world and that mages are one-in-a-million. I think that the vast majority of the 'magic' that occurs in WoD is Numina. I do not mind, however, Numina practitioners being one out of five hundred (0.2%) of the population.</div> </div> </div> </div>In ascension general Aleph managed to assemble 3000-4000 technocrats for war,and there were still more who didn't answered the call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T00:18:41-07:00","id":959130,"title":"","content":"Page 78 of ascension<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Aleph commands 4000 enlightened technocrats, 8000 extraordinary citizens and 20000 sleeper soldiers. He has no other reserves. This is an all-or-nothing fight to which he commits every technocrat that he can muster&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:39:36-07:00","id":961113,"title":"","content":"I think Marauder's % of the population should be very low 1% or 0.1%, so that the setting actually makes sense. <br /> <br /> Also Re: Malcom's numbers, I think Marauders and Nephandi are assumed to be jointly distributed through the rest of the Mage population and not an isolated faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T07:28:39-07:00","id":1073712,"title":"","content":"1:150,000 seems most reasonable. Because that is the figure authors confirmed in books. Explicitly.<br /> <br /> It is also concordant with figures given in revised books.<br /> <br /> And this should not be equated with &quot;the world is malleable&quot;. After all, most of Mages are relatively &quot;weak&quot; ones. Below Arete 3. Arete 4 to 5 at the most, I will say. These mages could not readily impose their Will on reality, let alone command or warp it.<br /> <br /> Still, I wonder why the Technocracy could only manage to muster 3,000 to 4,000 mages and twice sorcerers. Even if we apply 1:200,000 or even 1:250,000 in place of 1:150,000 there should be a lot more, probably tens of thousands of technocrat instead of a paltry thousands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 04-05-2017, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:12:34-07:00","id":1073728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=1073712#post1073712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I wonder why the Technocracy could only manage to muster 3,000 to 4,000 mages and twice sorcerers. Even if we apply 1:200,000 or even 1:250,000 in place of 1:150,000 there should be a lot more, probably tens of thousands of technocrat instead of a paltry thousands.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this number compare with the original idea that mages were around 1 in a million? (or something thereabouts... before it was changed to 1:150,000). Also, what year did this come out? Maybe I can extrapolate the numbers using that year's world population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:12:41-07:00","id":1073752,"title":"","content":"With around 7 000 000 000 of people in the world, and thus 7000 Mages, the Technocracy would have arround half of the lot. It seems coherent with that number. Twice Sorcerers work only if the original number doesn't include Sorcerers<br /> <br /> 1 : 1000 000 may sound impressive if every mage enlists to the war, but realistically you can't have the amount of subsects, and groups within the Traditions and the Technocracy with such numbers. Think about the amount of subgroups that the Order of Hermes have, with little more 300 mages. The Criamon are supposed to be near extint with &quot;only&quot; 30 mages, but that's almost 1/10 of the Tradition by these numbers! . With this number each cabal it's important, and you can't loose one mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:36:27-07:00","id":1073769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=1073752#post1073752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With around 7 000 000 000 of people in the world, and thus 7000 Mages, the Technocracy would have arround half of the lot. It seems coherent with that number. Twice Sorcerers work only if the original number doesn't include Sorcerers</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Technocracy wouldn't even have half of that mage population. There's more to the Mage society than the Tecnocratic Union and the Traditions. Sure, Orphans are rare and the crafts are all nearly dead (at least that's what everyone else thinks), but then there's als Nephandi (who could be mixed into the other groups, partly), a hand full of Marauders and maybe some other unaffiliated. Even though most factions seem more or less dead, it's because there is this really low number of awakened in the first place.<br /> Mages are rare. While Sorcerers aren't. If you think about it, every sleeper who has some kind of knowledge based around electronics or computers or whatever could be seen as a very low level Sorcerer (with a technocratic paradigm).<br /> <br /> Also, I think the rulebooks state quite clear, these are numbers as seen by factions! These are not the real, hard, total numbers but those that some mage or technocrat researched. There's surely some things he could have overlooked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:27:32-07:00","id":1073786,"title":"","content":"So these are the ballpark numbers I generally use (pulled from a WoD census file that was put together years ago, when the world population was about 6.5 billion). Since exact population numbers never really matter to a chronicle, it's worked well enough to give me starting number ideas whenever they are necessary.<br /> <br /> MAGES- 11,000ish (1 for 590,000 mortals) (There are two conflicting accounts. 1 in a million in a few older sources, and 1 in 150,000 mortals in Fallen Tower: Las Vegas. The first number doesn't leave enough mages for all their societies. The second, newer number incorporates all the sorcerers as well, which outnumber mages 3 to 1.)<br /> <br /> I think that strikes a decent balance between the numbers of Mages needed for their various organizations and the idea of them being at least a bit rare in general. Calculating from 7 billion people, the Mage population works out to just under 12,000. And since I think technocrats account for about 30% of the Mage population, that would give them around 3600 true Mages to call on (matching the numbers given in Ascension).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T17:37:44-07:00","id":1073941,"title":"","content":"Las Vegas only includes special snowflake sorcerers powerful enough to be considered as willworkers. So Las Vegas counts very few sorcerers as &quot;mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> And still, 1 for a million or 1 for 590,000 makes no sense to me. It is too few and simply not enough to exert global influence, alter and impose reality and hell, conduct and sustain Ascension War properly. Both the Tradition and the Technocracy, at least post-revised and M20 ones, are truly colossal organizations. And 7,000 or 11,000 Mages in the entire world is...improbable, disjointed, to say the least. In this regard, I completely agree with Ajax.<br /> <br /> For the same reason, I practically ignore 1 to 100,000 or more vampire rate. 1 to 50,000 or less is much more probable. In the same context, I also discard 1 to 500,000 shapeshifter count and instead use 1 to 200,000 or less.<br /> <br /> If you prefer fewer number, you can still use 1 to 200,000 or 1 to 250,000 figure given from other authors.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/156015-the-membership-numbers-of-the-traditions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...the-traditions</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 04-05-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T22:43:46-07:00","id":1075379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=1073786#post1073786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So these are the ballpark numbers I generally use (pulled from a WoD census file that was put together years ago, when the world population was about 6.5 billion). Since exact population numbers never really matter to a chronicle, it's worked well enough to give me starting number ideas whenever they are necessary.<br /> <br /> MAGES- 11,000ish (1 for 590,000 mortals) (There are two conflicting accounts. 1 in a million in a few older sources, and 1 in 150,000 mortals in Fallen Tower: Las Vegas. The first number doesn't leave enough mages for all their societies. The second, newer number incorporates all the sorcerers as well, which outnumber mages 3 to 1.)<br /> <br /> I think that strikes a decent balance between the numbers of Mages needed for their various organizations and the idea of them being at least a bit rare in general. Calculating from 7 billion people, the Mage population works out to just under 12,000. And since I think technocrats account for about 30% of the Mage population, that would give them around 3600 true Mages to call on (matching the numbers given in Ascension).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just meager 30%? That is too few...<br /> <br /> When considering everything, it is only reasonable to assess Technocracy gets the Lion's share of Awakened population on the Earth, or equally divides them between Traditions at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T23:26:54-07:00","id":1075383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/934774-mage-populations?p=1075379#post1075379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just meager 30%? That is too few...<br /> <br /> When considering everything, it is only reasonable to assess Technocracy gets the Lion's share of Awakened population on the Earth, or equally divides them between Traditions at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>To each their own.<br /> <br /> I put the Technocracy and Tradition both right around 1/3 of the Mage population (this is overall mind you, not just on Earth). That leaves the last third to be divided up among Orphans, the Nephandi, Marauders, the Crafts and Hollow Ones. I think that's about fair, given the setting setup. Obviously, YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}